[S]  YAAP  Link the neutral male doppelganger Monk

This is my first Slashem ascension.  I heard some people saying that
Slashem is harder than Nethack, so I decided to try Slashem.  My
favorite class in Nethack is monk, so I decided to try a monk in
Slashem.


Goal #1 is "get to XL 7 so the monk has 'Warning'.  I don't
know what new monsters are in Slashem, so I'm not going into the
Gnomish Mines until I get 'Warning'.  So I fought through the main
dungeon until I hit XL 7.

Goal #2 is "get the luckstone, and get the hard gems near the
luckstone".  This was very uneventful.  There was a noticeable lack
of mumaks, ants, or anything else that could have been threatening.  It
seems like Slashem replaced all of the threatening monsters with baby
dragons.  The baby dragons seemed easier to kill in Slashem than in
Nethack.

Goal #3 is "identify at least 2 hard gems".  I took my scrolls to
Minetown, and shop-IDed a scroll of identify.  So I read the scroll of
identify, and identified a small stack of hard gems.

Goal #4 is "throw 2 hard gems at a co-aligned unicorn".  I met a
co-aligned unicorn before I got the luckstone, so this goal happened
very quickly.

Goal #5 is "hope Sokoban has an amulet of reflection".  Sokoban had
a bag of holding.  Bags of holding are not useful in the early game.
Amulets of reflection can prevent a YASD.  Bags of holding do not
prevent YASDs.

Goal #6 is "get stuff from the Black Market".  I gathered a bunch
of stuff near the top-left corner of the Black Market, polymorphed into
a Xorn, and walked out of the Black Market.  That was very
non-threatening.

Goal #7 is "collect all the potions/books/scrolls/rings/amulets, and
bring them to the Minetown altar".  So far, I have IDed the scroll of
identify and the ring of levitation.  The only reason why I IDed the
ring of levitation is because it auto-IDs when you wear it.  All the
other potions/books/scrolls/rings/amulets are unidentified.  So I
dumped everything on the altar.  Then I blessed some scrolls of
identification, and IDed all of this stuff.

Goal #8 is "boost AC".  I had collected a very large amount of
'enchant armor' scrolls, so this was easy.

Goal #9 is "get a large stack of enchanted poisoned darts".  I did
not see any potions of sickness in my giant pile of stuff.  So I
randomly mixed potions together until I got a potion of sickness.

Goal #10 is "get drain resistance, get reflection, and get free
action".   I really need these things before a YASD happens.  So I
took my pickaxe, and dug down to Medusa's level.  Then I went down to
the castle.  Then I got the wand of wishing.  Then I wished for the
things that I needed.

Goal #11 is "do the side areas".  I did a couple of the side areas,
and found a very-very large amount of spellbooks.  When I first started
Slashem, I was worried because polymorphed items do not last forever.
Between the Black Market and the side areas, there really is not any
reason why someone would need to polymorph items.

Goal #12 is "do the quests".  The first notable thing in the game
happened here.  One of the quests had a lot of lava.  I accidentally
stepped into the lava.  Then I typed '#youpoly'.  Then I signed on
IRC to find out if I have enough time to get a wand of cold out of my
bag.  Then I tried to cancel the '#youpoly', and the game decided
to randomly turn me into a glowing eye.  So I used #youpoly to turn
back into a monk.  Then I got the wand of cold out of my bag.  Then I
froze the lava.

Goal #13 is "collect gold to donate".  I have not donated yet, so I
collected a bunch of gold, and donated it.

Goal #14 is "get shock resistance".  I don't have shock
resistance yet.  I ate 2 shock resistance rings, but neither of them
conferred shock resistance.  So I camped the altar until I got crowned.

Goal #15 is "get the candelabrum from Vlad's tower". I couldn't
figure out how to open the doors in Vlad's tower.  I had the 'Key
of Law' and the 'Key of Neutrality', but neither of them fit any
of the doors.  I signed on IRC to ask if there is anything special that
I should be doing.  It turned out that I was so tired, that I
couldn't figure out how to open doors.  The next day, I was able to
open the doors.

Goal #16 is "get the amulet".  The only notable thing along the way
is the zoo.  Before I reached the zoo, everything was awake.  This
never happened in Nethack, so I am not sure why everything was awake.
In the zoo, something was spamming "summon nasties".  I used
'charm monster', 'confused scrolls of charging', and a 'ring
of conflict'.  Eventually, I got tired of the zoo, so I just bashed a
narrow path through the monsters.  After I get the Book, I will have to
bash a path through the zoo again.  However, it is much faster to bash
a path twice, than it is to clear out the entire zoo once.

Goal #17 is "#offer the amulet".  Is there supposed to be something
different between the planes in Slashem and the planes in Nethack?  I
didn't notice anything new.  I ran through the planes so fast, that
maybe I missed the new stuff?  The only new thing I learned is that
wands of digging can anger the high priests.  I was using wands of
digging to open doors, and 2 of the high priests got angered from the
wands.


